 28 ### 1. `internal/core/ports/git.go`
 29 
 30 **Qué hacer:** Añadir tres métodos nuevos a la interfaz `Git`.
 31 
 32 Los tres métodos van justo después de `Commit(message string) (string, error)` en la sección `--- Write ---`:
 33 
 34 ```go
 35 // WriteTree captures the current staging area as an immutable tree object.
 36 // Returns the tree hash (SHA1). Fails if staging is empty.
 37 WriteTree() (string, error)
 38 
 39 // CommitTree creates a commit object pointing to treeHash with parentHash as parent.
 40 // Returns the new commit hash. parentHash is typically the current HEAD.
 41 CommitTree(treeHash, parentHash, message string) (string, error)
 42 
 43 // UpdateRef moves a ref (e.g. "HEAD") to point to commitHash.
 44 UpdateRef(ref, commitHash string) (string, error)
 45 ```
 46 
 47 **Por qué:** La interfaz define el contrato. El adapter implementa. El workflow llama por la interfaz. Sin esto nada compila.
